.TH SXCTL 1 "2026-08-13" "Sextant" "Sextant Manual"
.SH NAME
sxctl \- headless client for the Sextant fleet control plane
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sxctl
[\fB\-url\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-json\fR] \fIRESOURCE\fR \fIVERB\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sxctl
speaks the same HTTP API as the console (\fI/api/v1\fR) and nothing else.
Everything the console can do, it can do, and it authenticates the same
way \- with a token, never with a session. It holds no state of its own:
the fleet document in git is the state, and every write goes through the
same gate and audit trail as a change made in the browser.
.SH COMMANDS
.nf
  devices   list | get TAG | enroll TAG \-hardware H [\-group G] [\-class C] |
            update TAG [\-hardware H] [\-class C] [\-user U] [\-groups a,b] |
            retire TAG | reactivate TAG | remove TAG |
            lock TAG | wipe TAG [\-force] | unlock TAG
  groups    add NAME [\-parent P] [\-idp G] | update NAME [\-parent P|\-] [\-idp G] |
            remove NAME
  apps      set SCOPE KIND [NAME ...]   (kind: packages|flatpaks|overlays)
  settings  set SCOPE KEY VALUE [\-enforce] | clear SCOPE KEY
  changes   list | open ID TITLE | edit ID SCOPE KEY VALUE | diff ID |
            submit ID | merge ID | abandon ID
  rollout   status | start TARGET | tick | cancel
  status    [TAG]
  access    list | grant GROUP ROLE SCOPE | revoke GROUP SCOPE
  secrets   list | add NAME [\-description D] | remove NAME
            (secret REFERENCES \- the names settings point at, never values)
  tokens    list | mint NAME [\-ceiling R] [\-ttl\-days N] | revoke ID
  me        [prefs [TIMEZONE LOCALE]]   (who am I; get/set preferences)
  audit     (config commit trail)
  evidence  [FROM TO]   (audit bundle, RFC 3339; default last 30 days)
  fleet     get
.fi
.SH SCOPE
A scope is \fBorg\fR, \fBgroup:\fR\fINAME\fR or \fBdevice:\fR\fITAG\fR.
Values parse as JSON where they can (\fBtrue\fR, \fB42\fR, \fB"text"\fR)
and as a plain string otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-url " " \fIURL\fR
Base URL of the console. Defaults to \fBSEXTANT_URL\fR.
.TP
.B \-json
Emit JSON for list commands instead of the table meant for a terminal.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SEXTANT_URL
Base URL of the console, when \fB\-url\fR is not given.
.TP
.B SEXTANT_TOKEN
API token. Required. Read from the environment on purpose: a secret
passed on the command line is visible in the process table and in shell
history to everybody on the machine.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
The command was understood and the server refused it, or the request failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown resource or verb, missing argument, or missing
\fBSEXTANT_URL\fR / \fBSEXTANT_TOKEN\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
export SEXTANT_URL=https://console.example.org SEXTANT_TOKEN=...
sxctl devices list
sxctl settings set group:pilot desktop \(dqgnome\(dq
sxctl changes open raise\-poll \(dqraise the poll interval\(dq
sxctl changes submit raise\-poll
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The API contract this speaks is published at \fI/api/v1/openapi.json\fR
on any console, and the handbook at \fIhttps://docs.sextantfleet.com\fR.
